    "notes": "Concurrency sweep, two shapes on one server: long 512 in / 128 out and short 128 in / 512 out, concurrency 1,2,4,8,16, 3 repeats per level. Every level ran only after a >=60 s cooldown with the CPU package <=50 C and the GPU <=45 C (driver.log). Server -c 16384 --parallel 16 (1024 tokens per slot). 32 slots does NOT fit on E4B: llama.cpp allocates each slot its own 1024-cell sliding-window KV (40 MiB/slot), so -c 32768 --parallel 32 failed to allocate 1280 MiB (probe/). Prompt cache VERIFIED defeated: prompt_tokens_cached_total 0 of 65,830. Thinking ON per request (sweep.py asks for it). Arm attested gpu, sha256 9f2a8b0b6ed5365d, model the E4B exact file. llama.cpp f95b0d9, -t 6 -tb 12. Not comparable to the E2B rig's 2026-09-03/09-08 concurrency runs as a model comparison: those were on 95ef7fc, -t 4, without cooldown gating (09-03) and with -c 32768 --parallel 32 (09-03)."
